<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuan Shikai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1859–1916</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuan Shikai was a Chinese general who built the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-army">Beiyang Army</a> under the Qing. In 1912 he arranged the abdication of the last emperor and became President of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, then dissolved parliament and ruled as a dictator. His attempt to make himself emperor in 1915–1916 provoked revolt, and he died in June 1916.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai.jpg" alt="Yuan Shikai" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo by Rio V. De Sieux [1] · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YuanShikaiPresidente1915.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
